      "explain": "Regular four-way harmony; *o* adds an n, *onu*. The plural keeps its *-lar*: *onları*."
    },
    {
      "id": "a1-u08-l03-e02",
      "type": "mcq",
      "points": ["gp-pronoun-accusative", "gp-present-continuous"],
      "question": "How do you say **I miss you**?",
      "options": ["Seni özlüyorum.", "Sen özlüyorum.", "Sana özlüyorum.", "Seni özlüyorsun."],
      "optionsLang": "tr",
      "answer": 0,
      "why": {
        "1": "A pronoun object always takes the accusative: *seni*.",
        "2": "*Özlemek* takes a direct object, not the dative.",
        "3": "*Özlüyorsun* means **you** miss."
      },
      "explain": "*Sen* + `-i` = *seni*; *özle-* drops its e before `-Iyor`: *özlüyorum*."
    },
    {
      "id": "a1-u08-l03-e03",
      "type": "translate",
      "from": "tr",
      "points": ["gp-pronoun-accusative"],
      "prompt": "Beni duyuyor musun?",
      "accept": ["Can you hear me?", "Do you hear me?"]
    },
    {
      "id": "a1-u08-l03-e04",
      "type": "cloze",
      "points": ["gp-pronoun-accusative"],
      "text": "Kim___ bekliyorsun?",
      "en": "Who are you waiting for?",
      "blanks": [
        {
          "accept": ["i"],
          "reject": [
            {
              "answer": "e",
              "why": "*Kime* means **to whom**. *Beklemek* takes a direct object: *kimi*."
            },
            {
              "answer": "den",
              "why": "*Kimden* means **from whom**. *Beklemek* takes a direct object: *kimi*."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "explain": "*Beklemek* takes a direct object, and a person is definite: *kimi bekliyorsun?*"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1-u08-l03-e05",
      "type": "listen",
